    <h2>We are fierce trial ready advocates for our injured clients with a track record built in the courtroom.</h2>
    <p>Many personal injury firms settle quickly to avoid the work of trial preparation. We take a different approach. Our verdicts and settlements reflect decades of fighting for injured clients throughout Michigan—in Washtenaw, Wayne, Livingston, Jackson, and Calhoun counties. When insurance companies see our name on a case, they know we're prepared to go the distance. That preparation shows in our results, from a $5.1 million verdict for a woman killed by a semi truck to a $1.3 million malicious prosecution award against a township that abused its authority.</p>

    <h3>Fighting Insurance Company Denials</h3>
    <p>Insurance companies routinely deny legitimate claims, hoping injured people will give up. They argue that injuries stem from "unrelated" conditions, that treatment is "unnecessary," or that coverage doesn't apply. We've heard every excuse—and we've beaten them. Our results include a $2 million settlement for a traumatic brain injury victim whose insurer denied all benefits, a $1 million verdict against Amerisure for a man they fought for 18 years, and jury awards against Allstate, State Farm, Farmers, and Auto-Owners when they refused to pay for the care our clients needed.</p>

    <h3>No-Fault Benefits Your Insurer Owes You</h3>
    <p>Michigan's no-fault system entitles accident victims to coverage for medical expenses, attendant care, and home modifications—but collecting those benefits often requires a fight. We've recovered millions in first-party claims, securing not just past-due benefits but future coverage for clients who need ongoing care. From a $730,000 settlement against Esurance to lifetime medical coverage awarded by a Washtenaw County jury, we make sure insurers honor their obligations.</p>

    <h2>Here's a few of our recent verdicts and settlements:</h2>

